 {
  "type": "tweet",
  "id": "2113094732666593360",
  "url": "https://x.com/ffdataroma/status/2113094732666593360",
  "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/ffdataroma/status/2113094732666593360",
  "text": "Have seen multiple accounts cite JJ McCarthys\u2019s catchable throw rate being poor, but that\u2019s just completely false.\n\nFiltering out spikes, he was at a 76.5% catchable throw rate, which was 14th of 29 QBs in Week 6 (and would be 16th of 34 QBs on the year).\n\nAnd on top of that, his average depth of target was 15.24 yards downfield. That\u2019s extremely deep, nearly 5 (!) yards deeper than the 2nd highest QB on the year. Target depth is obviously going to be directly correlated catchable throw rate, so that 76.5% catchable rate is actually quite good considering aDOT.\n\nNot to suggest JJ is good because of 1 strong quarter in garbage time, and he\u2019s likely still a bad QB for that matter given what we saw in his 1st year. But let\u2019s give credit where it\u2019s due, JJ played well last week. And throwing around random stats without understanding the context behind them helps no one.",
